  <circuit name="diy-wave-generator">
    <a name="appearance" val="classic"/>
    <comp lib="0" loc="(1014,446)" name="Callout">
      <a name="dx" val="-20"/>
      <a name="dy" val="22"/>
      <a name="foreground" val="#f56224"/>
      <a name="text" val="Input, Signed Decimal (32 bit)"/>
    </comp>
    <comp lib="0" loc="(221,204)" name="Text">
      <a name="background" val="#f7a2da6e"/>
      <a name="text">(1) Put a register
in the middle, to
keep track of 
the current number.
Or use a few
registers, each
serving as a variable. </a>
    </comp>
    <comp lib="0" loc="(30,24)" name="Text">
      <a name="text">Your circuit goes here...

Do some arithmetic and feedback loops with 32 bit numbers.
These have a big range (-2 billion to +2 billion).
But aim to have numbers varying between about -10000 and +10000,
and try to make them oscillate rapidly (anywhere from a few times 
per second, to a few hundred times per second).

The clock will tick 16000 times per second.</a>
    </comp>
    <comp lib="0" loc="(36,205)" name="Text">
      <a name="background" val="#7ff7576e"/>
      <a name="text">(2) Generate new
values, by feeding
the old values into
some equation. You can
encorporate random
numbers too, or 
also include user-input
as part of the equation.</a>
    </comp>
    <comp lib="0" loc="(397,214)" name="Text">
      <a name="background" val="#78b9f76e"/>
      <a name="text">(3) Send one
of the values
to the audio output.
Or use a combination
of several values.</a>
    </comp>
    <comp lib="0" loc="(624,804)" name="Callout">
      <a name="dx" val="-66"/>
      <a name="dy" val="-133"/>
      <a name="foreground" val="#f56224"/>
      <a name="text">This converts an 8-bit number
within [0, 255] so it
falls between -5000 and 5000
as a 32-bit number.</a>
    </comp>
    <comp lib="0" loc="(701,406)" name="Callout">
      <a name="dx" val="-20"/>
      <a name="dy" val="22"/>
      <a name="foreground" val="#f56224"/>
      <a name="text" val="Constants."/>
    </comp>
    <comp lib="0" loc="(80,439)" name="Text">
      <a name="background" val="#f7b1216e"/>
      <a name="text">(optional) Use some user
input (dial, slider, input)
to affect the calculation
in some way.</a>
    </comp>
    <comp lib="0" loc="(904,326)" name="Callout">
      <a name="dx" val="-20"/>
      <a name="dy" val="22"/>
      <a name="foreground" val="#f56224"/>
      <a name="text" val="Input, 32-bit binary"/>
    </comp>
    <comp lib="1" loc="(1040,490)" name="Pin">
      <a name="radix" val="10signed"/>
      <a name="width" val="32"/>
    </comp>
    <comp lib="1" loc="(1040,530)" name="Pin">
