  <circuit name="diy-sine-wave">
    <comp lib="0" loc="(146,647)" name="Callout">
      <a name="dx" val="94"/>
      <a name="dy" val="-8"/>
      <a name="foreground" val="#0400fa"/>
      <a name="text">Using k=2 and m=5000
works well</a>
    </comp>
    <comp lib="0" loc="(23,43)" name="Text">
      <a name="text">Goal: generate an audio wave by simulating a "mass and spring" system. Just picture a
baseball, suspended from the ceiling by a spring. When perfectly balanced, the ball will
be at rest, not bouncing at all. Call that position X=0. If we give it a push to displace it
upwards (making X positive) or downwards (making X negative), it will react by vibrating,
oscillating up and down. The varying position, X, over time will be our audio signal: we
will essentially be listening the the vibrations of the mass on a spring.

Physics notes: Position is X, velocity is Xd (in units of distance per clock tick), and the
spring is pulling back towards the origin with force X*k/m, where k is the spring
constant and m is the mass. After 1 clock tick, Xd changes by by -X*k/m, so the new
velocity Xd' after 1 clock tick will be:
    Xd' = Xd + X*(-k)/m
And X changes depending on the velocity, so the new position after 1 clock tick will be:
   X' = X + Xd'
The overall frequency of oscillation will be sqrt(k/m), in units of oscillations per clock tick.
If we are running at 16kHz clock rate, then freq = 16000*sqrt(k/m) Hz.</a>
    </comp>
    <comp lib="0" loc="(258,650)" name="Text">
      <a name="text" val="k"/>
    </comp>
    <comp lib="0" loc="(302,420)" name="Callout">
      <a name="dx" val="21"/>
      <a name="dy" val="59"/>
      <a name="foreground" val="#0400fa"/>
      <a name="text">X times (negative k)
divided by m</a>
    </comp>
    <comp lib="0" loc="(336,652)" name="Text">
      <a name="text" val="m"/>
    </comp>
    <comp lib="1" loc="(140,420)" name="Clock">
      <a name="facing" val="north"/>
    </comp>
    <comp lib="1" loc="(140,540)" name="Clock">
      <a name="facing" val="north"/>
    </comp>
    <comp lib="1" loc="(260,620)" name="Constant">
      <a name="facing" val="north"/>
      <a name="radix" val="10signed"/>
      <a name="value" val="0x00000002"/>
      <a name="width" val="32"/>
    </comp>
    <comp lib="1" loc="(340,620)" name="Constant">
      <a name="facing" val="north"/>
      <a name="radix" val="10signed"/>
      <a name="value" val="0x00001388"/>
      <a name="width" val="32"/>
    </comp>
    <comp lib="1" loc="(570,540)" name="Clock">
